NILAVARAM COMMAND AND CREDENTIAL REFERENCE

CLASP

clasp --version
  Shows the installed clasp version.

clasp status
  Shows which local files are linked to Apps Script.

clasp push
  Uploads the current Apps Script source files.

The project link is stored in .clasp.json. The personal .clasprc.json OAuth
credential file is stored outside the repository and must never be shared,
displayed in the UI or committed.

GIT AND GITHUB

git status
git add .
git commit -m "Clear milestone description"
git pull --rebase origin main
git push origin main
git remote -v

GitHub authentication belongs in Git or the operating-system credential
manager. Never save a GitHub password or access token in project files.

FIRESTORE

The Firestore Project ID is read from the Apps Script Property:
FIRESTORE_PROJECT_ID

Firestore requests use temporary Google OAuth access tokens. Never copy those
tokens into project notes or the user interface.

